Signs you have reached your ceiling in a section for the day:

- your **last few attempts were two-option guesses**, not solved questions;
- your running **accuracy is sliding** and each new attempt is harder than the last;
- everything left is a long set you have already judged not worth the time.

At that point, on a **single overall clock**, the marginal minute is better spent banking easy marks in another section. Under **fixed sectional timing**, you cannot move the time, so spend the remainder rechecking flagged answers you actually reasoned out - not blind-filling.

Stopping is a decision, not a failure. A section cleared at its cut-off with room to spare has done its job.
